  "notes": "{覚|さ}ます is a transitive godan verb meaning to wake someone, or figuratively to dispel an illusion or intoxication.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{覚|さ}める→覚める：02058_sameru⟧ (intransitive — to wake up, to wear off)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{覚|さ}まして⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means \"is (in the process of) waking someone\" or \"is sobering up.\"\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{覚|さ}ます: to wake up (literally \"to open one's eyes\")\n- ⟦{酔|よ}い→酔う：14437_you⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{覚|さ}ます: to sober up\n- ⟦{夢|ゆめ}→夢：01519_yume⟧⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧{覚|さ}ます: to wake from a dream\n- ⟦{現実|げんじつ}→現実：02720_genjitsu⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{覚|さ}ます: to wake up to reality\n- ⟦{興奮|こうふん}→興奮：02751_koufun⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{覚|さ}ます: to calm down from excitement\n\nUSAGE:\nThe expression ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{覚|さ}ます can be both literal (waking from sleep) and figurative (coming to one's senses). Do not confuse with ⟦{冷|さ}ます→冷ます：02113_samasu⟧ (to cool down — different kanji).",
